<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Arsuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1191">1191</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> was fought in 1191 on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s forces. The Crusaders won, allowing them to secure <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>. The battle checked Saladin, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> kept control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-arsuf.jpg" alt="Battle of Arsuf" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Éloi Firmin Féron · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_von_Arsuf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
